WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.390
A Catholic parish church in the 1950s.

2
00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:08.070
The altar stands against the
far wall, and Mass is in Latin.

3
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:10.600
Step into the same church today.

4
00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:13.400
The altar stands free, facing the people,

5
00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.590
and the Mass is in English.

6
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:18.610
Between those two pictures sits one event:

7
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:23.830
the Second Vatican
Council, from 1962 to 1965.

8
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:29.740
So why did a meeting of bishops change what
Sunday Mass looks like in every parish?

9
00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:32.660
In this mission, you'll
follow the Council's story,

10
00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:37.280
from a surprise announcement
in 1959 to 1965.

11
00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:41.910
Then you'll meet its four key documents,
each one named after its first words

12
00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.160
in Latin.

13
00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:48.930
Your mission: find out why a meeting of
bishops changed Sunday Mass in every parish.
